{"id":"cybersecurity-basics","title":"What is cybersecurity?","subject":"Cybersecurity","label":"Cybersecurity","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":182,"duration":181.57,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":463,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":13.485},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":13.485,"end":45.725},{"id":"explain2","title":"Attack routes","start":45.725,"end":83.675},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":83.675,"end":115.925},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":115.925,"end":123.745},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":123.745,"end":130.295},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":130.295,"end":155.165},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":155.165,"end":181.57}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":6.43,"text":"Your phone buzzes. A message says your bank account is locked, and asks you to tap a link. Should you trust it?","w":[0.52,0.68,0.94,1.74,1.84,2.22,2.44,2.6,2.84,3.16,3.3,3.98,4.2,4.46,4.6,4.7,4.96,5.06,5.74,5.94,6.04,6.32]},{"s":0,"a":6.88,"b":9.32,"text":"I'm Kora, and this is cybersecurity.","w":[7,7.2,7.98,8.14,8.36,8.48]},{"s":0,"a":9.62,"b":13.06,"text":"In three minutes, you'll know what it is and how to defend yourself.","w":[9.66,9.84,10.12,10.72,10.98,11.16,11.34,11.48,11.9,12.06,12.26,12.38,12.68]},{"s":1,"a":13.91,"b":18.65,"text":"Cybersecurity means protecting your devices, your networks and your data from harm.","w":[14.08,14.96,15.24,15.72,15.86,16.72,16.92,17.56,17.66,17.82,18.12,18.3]},{"s":1,"a":18.95,"b":23.68,"text":"It has three goals. The first is confidentiality: private things stay private.","w":[19,19.1,19.32,19.58,20.46,20.58,20.94,21.1,22.36,22.76,23.06,23.3]},{"s":1,"a":23.98,"b":26.51,"text":"For example, a private chat stays private.","w":[24,24.18,24.86,24.98,25.38,25.72,26.04]},{"s":1,"a":26.81,"b":31.45,"text":"The second is integrity: information is correct and not changed by anyone else.","w":[26.84,27,27.4,27.54,28.58,29.14,29.28,29.9,30.04,30.26,30.6,30.82,31.16]},{"s":1,"a":31.75,"b":34.88,"text":"For example, your exam result is not changed.","w":[31.82,32.04,33,33.22,33.6,34.02,34.16,34.4]},{"s":1,"a":35.18,"b":39.15,"text":"The third is availability: systems and data are there when you need them.","w":[35.18,35.34,35.64,35.78,37.12,37.58,37.72,38.06,38.2,38.48,38.62,38.74,38.92]},{"s":1,"a":39.45,"b":42.62,"text":"For example, your banking app works when you need it.","w":[39.5,39.72,40.72,40.98,41.4,41.58,42.04,42.2,42.32,42.5]},{"s":1,"a":42.92,"b":45.3,"text":"Together, these are the C I A triad.","w":[42.92,43.5,43.76,43.88,44.06,44.42,44.58,44.8]},{"s":2,"a":46.15,"b":48.91,"text":"Attacks usually start with four common weaknesses.","w":[46.2,46.8,47.16,47.44,47.64,47.94,48.26]},{"s":2,"a":49.21,"b":55.06,"text":"One is tricking a person, often called phishing. It often arrives as a message pretending to be your bank.","w":[49.38,49.54,49.74,50.08,50.16,50.86,51.18,51.48,52.4,52.58,52.84,53.26,53.38,53.48,53.86,54.32,54.42,54.54,54.72]},{"s":2,"a":55.36,"b":59.32,"text":"Another is a weak password, or the same password reused everywhere.","w":[55.46,55.82,55.94,56.04,56.3,57.22,57.36,57.52,57.8,58.32,58.86]},{"s":2,"a":59.62,"b":62.09,"text":"Another is software that was never updated.","w":[59.72,60.18,60.32,60.92,61.08,61.28,61.6]},{"s":2,"a":62.39,"b":65.38,"text":"The last is malware, harmful software running on a device.","w":[62.42,62.56,62.94,63.08,63.52,63.9,64.4,64.68,64.78,64.86]},{"s":2,"a":65.68,"b":68.83,"text":"Attackers look for the easiest way in, not the hardest.","w":[65.76,66.36,66.6,66.72,66.98,67.36,67.64,67.98,68.18,68.32]},{"s":2,"a":69.13,"b":71.62,"text":"Touching systems without permission is illegal.","w":[69.18,69.54,70.06,70.38,71,71.2]},{"s":2,"a":71.92,"b":76.47,"text":"We defend in layers. Use strong unique passwords and two step verification.","w":[71.94,72.16,72.52,72.64,73.48,73.66,74.06,74.32,75,75.18,75.42,75.7]},{"s":2,"a":76.77,"b":80.31,"text":"Update your software, keep backups, and think before you click.","w":[76.86,77.2,77.38,78.2,78.48,79.16,79.34,79.6,79.88,80.02]},{"s":2,"a":80.61,"b":83.25,"text":"One missed defence should not expose everything.","w":[80.78,81,81.32,81.96,82.2,82.36,82.84]},{"s":3,"a":84.1,"b":87.82,"text":"A student gets a text saying their bank account is locked, with a link.","w":[84.14,84.22,84.6,84.82,84.9,85.32,85.6,85.78,86.04,86.36,86.5,87.32,87.5,87.58]},{"s":3,"a":88.12,"b":93.3,"text":"The message is not from the bank at all. The link is designed to trick them into giving details.","w":[88.2,88.34,88.8,88.94,89.14,89.3,89.42,89.7,89.86,90.5,90.66,90.92,91.04,91.56,91.74,92,92.2,92.42,92.68]},{"s":3,"a":93.6,"b":98.83,"text":"Which goal is at risk? Confidentiality, because private banking details could be stolen.","w":[93.64,93.92,94.22,94.36,94.52,95.34,96.64,96.98,97.38,97.72,98.16,98.32,98.44]},{"s":3,"a":99.13,"b":102.73,"text":"Availability is also at risk if the real account gets locked.","w":[99.2,99.92,100.16,100.48,100.62,101.28,101.4,101.54,101.78,102.12,102.38]},{"s":3,"a":103.03,"b":107.51,"text":"Defences stop it: do not click. Contact the bank using its official number.","w":[103.03,103.52,103.84,104.3,104.46,104.68,105.48,105.96,106.08,106.46,106.7,106.84,107.2]},{"s":3,"a":107.81,"b":112.21,"text":"Two step verification helps, because a stolen password alone is not enough.","w":[107.86,108.14,108.44,109.14,109.9,110.24,110.36,110.8,111.24,111.62,111.76,111.96]},{"s":3,"a":112.51,"b":115.5,"text":"Updates and backups protect against other attacks too.","w":[112.6,113.12,113.28,113.8,114.2,114.56,114.78,115.2]},{"s":4,"a":116.35,"b":120.57,"text":"Quick check. If a website leaks your private chat, which goal is harmed?","w":[116.38,116.66,117.38,117.52,117.6,118.1,118.34,118.52,118.88,119.54,119.78,120.08,120.18]},{"s":4,"a":121.02,"b":123.32,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[121.08,121.4,121.7,121.86,122.16,122.84,123.04]},{"s":5,"a":124.17,"b":129.87,"text":"The answer is confidentiality. The chat was meant to stay private, and a leak breaks that promise.","w":[124.18,124.38,124.72,124.88,126.3,126.44,126.74,126.9,127.08,127.18,127.42,128.28,128.42,128.52,128.8,129.12,129.32]},{"s":6,"a":130.72,"b":137.36,"text":"Common mistake one: using the same password everywhere. If one site leaks, every account is exposed.","w":[130.78,131.14,131.62,132.48,132.72,132.88,133.18,133.76,134.82,135.06,135.24,135.52,136.08,136.34,136.68,136.82]},{"s":6,"a":137.66,"b":141.42,"text":"Use unique passwords, and let a password manager remember them.","w":[137.82,138.04,138.38,139.46,139.62,139.82,139.9,140.36,140.8,141.18]},{"s":6,"a":141.72,"b":147.15,"text":"Common mistake two: ignoring updates. Updates often close known security holes.","w":[141.78,142.2,142.64,143.26,143.8,144.7,145.22,145.56,145.92,146.22,146.72]},{"s":6,"a":147.45,"b":149.62,"text":"Turn on automatic updates where you can.","w":[147.5,147.78,148.02,148.54,148.94,149.12,149.26]},{"s":6,"a":149.92,"b":154.74,"text":"Common mistake three: clicking before thinking. Slow down and check the sender.","w":[149.98,150.3,150.7,151.42,151.78,152.12,153.06,153.38,153.78,153.94,154.22,154.36]},{"s":7,"a":155.59,"b":160.09,"text":"Recap. Cybersecurity protects devices, networks and data.","w":[155.64,156.68,157.58,157.98,158.94,159.6,159.74]},{"s":7,"a":160.39,"b":164.2,"text":"The three goals are confidentiality, integrity and availability.","w":[160.44,160.62,160.92,161.38,161.54,162.78,163.42,163.54]},{"s":7,"a":164.5,"b":171.51,"text":"Defend in layers with unique passwords, two step verification, updates, backups and careful clicking.","w":[164.5,165.12,165.28,165.7,165.92,166.3,167.24,167.5,167.82,168.96,169.74,170.48,170.68,171.1]},{"s":7,"a":171.81,"b":176.45,"text":"Top tip: pause before you click, because one calm check can stop an attack.","w":[171.84,172.16,172.78,173.2,173.5,173.62,174.32,174.68,174.88,175.18,175.58,175.78,176.04,176.14]},{"s":7,"a":176.75,"b":180.97,"text":"Knowzone is here to help you learn safely, one clear step at a time.","w":[176.88,177.54,177.66,177.9,178.02,178.22,178.36,178.66,179.66,179.88,180.18,180.42,180.52,180.6]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Bank account locked? Tap a link?"},{"at":6.78,"kind":"text","text":"I'm Kora: cybersecurity"},{"at":9.52,"kind":"text","text":"Know what it is and how to defend yourself"}]},{"at":13.66,"heading":"Core idea","items":[{"at":13.81,"kind":"term","text":"Cybersecurity","detail":"Protecting devices, networks and data from harm"},{"at":18.85,"kind":"term","text":"Confidentiality","detail":"Private things stay private"},{"at":23.88,"kind":"text","text":"Private chat stays private"},{"at":26.71,"kind":"term","text":"Integrity","detail":"Information is correct and not changed by others"}]},{"at":31.5,"heading":"CIA triad","items":[{"at":31.65,"kind":"text","text":"Exam result is not changed"},{"at":35.08,"kind":"term","text":"Availability","detail":"Systems and data are there when you need them"},{"at":39.35,"kind":"text","text":"Banking app works when needed"},{"at":42.82,"kind":"text","text":"CIA triad: confidentiality, integrity, availability"},{"at":42.82,"kind":"image","text":"The CIA triad: the three goals of security","src":"triad.webp","credit":"Michel Bakni · CC BY-SA 4.0 · Wikimedia Commons"}]},{"at":45.9,"heading":"Attack routes","items":[{"at":46.05,"kind":"text","text":"Attacks start with common weaknesses"},{"at":49.11,"kind":"term","text":"Phishing","detail":"Fake message tricks a person"},{"at":55.26,"kind":"term","text":"Weak password","detail":"Weak or reused everywhere"},{"at":59.52,"kind":"text","text":"Software never updated"},{"at":62.29,"kind":"term","text":"Malware","detail":"Harmful software running on a device"}]},{"at":65.43,"heading":"Defences in layers","items":[{"at":65.58,"kind":"text","text":"Attackers pick the easiest way in"},{"at":69.03,"kind":"text","text":"Unauthorised access is illegal"},{"at":71.82,"kind":"text","text":"Strong unique passwords + 2-step verification"},{"at":76.67,"kind":"text","text":"Update, backup, think before clicking"},{"at":80.51,"kind":"text","text":"Layers: one missed defence should not expose all"}]},{"at":83.85,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":84,"kind":"text","text":"Student gets bank-lock text with link"},{"at":88.02,"kind":"text","text":"Not from bank; link steals details"},{"at":93.5,"kind":"term","text":"Confidentiality","detail":"Banking details could be stolen"},{"at":99.03,"kind":"term","text":"Availability","detail":"Real account could get locked"},{"at":102.93,"kind":"text","text":"Do not click; call bank official number"}]},{"at":107.56,"heading":"Defences","items":[{"at":107.71,"kind":"text","text":"2-step verification: stolen password not enough"},{"at":112.41,"kind":"text","text":"Updates and backups protect against other attacks"}]},{"at":115.92,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":115.92,"kind":"question","text":"If a website leaks your private chat, which goal is harmed?"}]},{"at":123.92,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":124.07,"kind":"term","text":"Confidentiality","detail":"Private chat leaked; privacy broken"},{"at":124.07,"kind":"text","text":"Leak breaks the promise of privacy"}]},{"at":130.47,"heading":"Common mistakes 1","items":[{"at":130.62,"kind":"wrong","text":"Same password everywhere"},{"at":137.56,"kind":"tip","text":"Let a password manager remember them for you"}]},{"at":141.47,"heading":"Common mistakes 2","items":[{"at":141.62,"kind":"wrong","text":"Ignoring updates"},{"at":149.82,"kind":"wrong","text":"Clicking before thinking"}]},{"at":155.34,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":155.49,"kind":"text","text":"Cybersecurity protects devices, networks and data"},{"at":160.29,"kind":"text","text":"Goals: confidentiality, integrity, availability"},{"at":164.4,"kind":"text","text":"Layers: unique passwords, 2-step, updates, backups, care"},{"at":171.71,"kind":"tip","text":"Pause before you click; one calm check can stop an attack"},{"at":176.65,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: learn safely, one clear step at a time"}]}],"check":{"at":123.57,"seconds":10,"question":"If a website leaks your private chat, which goal is harmed?","answer":"Confidentiality — the chat was meant to stay private."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[{"title":"CIAJMK1209-en.svg","author":"Michel Bakni","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CIAJMK1209-en.svg"}],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}